                                "sense_id": "c548690c-f603-3010-8ca1-55347f4e55bb",
                                "text": "April 1891, Robert Louis Stevenson, letter to Edmund Goose\nThere were two, or perhaps three, flabbinesses of style which (in your work) amazed me. Am I right in thinking you were a shade bored over the last chapters?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9a418ea1-013a-4a7a-8f60-6cd826ac83a8",
                                "sense_id": "c548690c-f603-3010-8ca1-55347f4e55bb",
                                "text": "Woona had silently and swiftly backed away; and her ebon face, Ursula saw, had changed into leaden flabbiness with some horrible fear."
                            }
                        ]
